The first factor is 47 880 − 32 500 = 15 380. Hmm, this puts the F state above 32 500, so H11 must be wrong. The correct ⁴T₁(F) diagonal is −Dq relative to F... \n\nThe corrected diagonal is H11 = 6Dq − 12Dq... The ⁴T₁(F) level sits at +3Dq relative to the ⁴F barycenter (⁴T₂ at −2Dq, ⁴A₂ at −12Dq, ⁴T₁ at +6Dq). Using ⁴T₂ = 10Dq gives ⁴T₂ at −2Dq, so ⁴T₁F is at +6Dq, which is 18Dq above ground. That is 47 880, far above the observed 32 500, so the observed value must come from the repulsion lowering it. The root is lowered strongly by mixing with ⁴T₁(P), and this fixes B.\n\nSolve (47 880 − 32 500)(15B + 6Dq − 32 500) = 36B², with 6Dq = 15 960:\n- 15 380(15B − 16 540) = 36B²\n- 36B² − 230 700B + 254 385 200 = 0\n- B = [230 700 − √(230 700² − 4·36·254 385 200)]/72\n- 230 700² = 5.3222×10¹⁰, and 4·36·254 385 200 = 3.6631×10¹⁰\n- The difference is 1.6591×10¹⁰, with square root 128 810\n- B = (230 700 − 128 810)/72 = 1415 cm⁻¹\n\nThis is too large for Cr(III) (the free ion is about 1030), so this is unreliable. The matrix I used is also not the correct one, and I cannot confirm it.\n\n**Finding C.** C would follow from the ²E energy, but it depends on B and on the correct matrix. Because B is unreliable, C is not trustworthy either.\n\nI could not derive B and C reliably, so I report only Dq.\n\n{\"Dq\": 2660, \"B\": null, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq = ν1/10 is direct, but my B and C derivation was not reliable, so I give no values for them.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":817,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":817,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aecd9d16-1e49-411e-8ac2-375d37c46522","uuid":"a56bf8d5-266